From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:56:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] linux: build with the flags of rv32-sim/apps/coremark

The port linux, which Buildroot builds for a 32-bit target, takes the
flags of rv32-sim/apps/coremark of the FonTamSOC, the bare-metal build
of CoreMark for its ftpu cores, after the PORT_CFLAGS which Buildroot
sets on the command line, so that -O3 overrides Buildroot's -O2, ie:
- -O3 -DMULTITHREAD=16, and the -DPERFORMANCE_RUN=1 of the target all
  of its Makefile, which SEED_ARG makes moot here, but which CoreMark
  prints among the flags;
- EXTRA_CFLAGS, its tuning of the optimizations of GCC, as is;
- -g -fstack-usage -fdata-sections -ffunction-sections
  -Wl,--gc-sections.

Save three:
- -DUSE__OS=1, whose contexts are threads of underLineOS, gives way to
  -DUSE_PTHREAD=1 -pthread, the threads of pthreads, which the port
  implements: without MMU, fork() is not available;
- -specs=nano.specs, which selects newlib-nano, is left out: uClibc-ng
  has no such spec file;
- -Wl,-z,max-page-size=4, which lays out a bare-metal ELF, is left out:
  elf2flt lays out the FLAT binary.

Upstream: N/A, specific to the FonTamSOC
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
---
 linux/core_portme.mak | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/linux/core_portme.mak b/linux/core_portme.mak
index 025b035..2d3cd62 100755
--- a/linux/core_portme.mak
+++ b/linux/core_portme.mak
@@ -9,8 +9,24 @@ CC = gcc
 # Flag: CFLAGS
 #	Use this flag to define compiler options. Note, you can add compiler options from the command line using XCFLAGS="other flags"
 PORT_CFLAGS = -O2
+# The flags of rv32-sim/apps/coremark of the FonTamSOC, the bare-metal build
+# of its ftpu cores, follow the PORT_CFLAGS which Buildroot sets on the
+# command line, so that -O3 overrides its -O2. Save three: -DUSE__OS=1, whose
+# contexts are threads of underLineOS, gives way to -DUSE_PTHREAD=1 -pthread;
+# -specs=nano.specs, which is newlib's, and -Wl,-z,max-page-size=4, which lays
+# out a bare-metal ELF, are left out. -DPERFORMANCE_RUN=1 is that of its target
+# all: SEED_ARG makes it moot here, but CoreMark prints it among the flags.
+override PORT_CFLAGS += -O3 -DMULTITHREAD=16 -DUSE_PTHREAD=1 -pthread -DPERFORMANCE_RUN=1
+EXTRA_CFLAGS = -mbranch-cost=2 -funroll-all-loops -finline-functions \
+	-finline-limit=10000 -fno-tree-sink -fselective-scheduling \
+	-fno-if-conversion2 -fno-code-hoisting -fno-strict-overflow \
+	-fira-region=one -falign-functions=4 \
+	-fsplit-paths -msmall-data-limit=1024 -fno-caller-saves \
+	-fno-split-loops -fno-tree-partial-pre -fno-version-loops-for-strides \
+	--param max-completely-peeled-insns=16 -fvect-cost-model=very-cheap
 FLAGS_STR = "$(PORT_CFLAGS) $(XCFLAGS) $(XLFLAGS) $(LFLAGS_END)"
-CFLAGS = $(PORT_CFLAGS) -I$(PORT_DIR) -I. -DFLAGS_STR=\"$(FLAGS_STR)\"
+CFLAGS = -g -fstack-usage -fdata-sections -ffunction-sections -Wl,--gc-sections \
+	$(PORT_CFLAGS) $(EXTRA_CFLAGS) -I$(PORT_DIR) -I. -DFLAGS_STR=\"$(FLAGS_STR)\"
 #Flag: LFLAGS_END
 #	Define any libraries needed for linking or other flags that should come at the end of the link line (e.g. linker scripts). 
 #	Note: On certain platforms, the default clock_gettime implementation is supported but requires linking of librt.
